f person(s) (cl. accusative; WM, § 32, 1 β), Luk.6:27; with accusative of thing(s), Mrk.7:37; with ptcp., Act.10:33 (M, Pr., 131), Php.4:14, 2Pe.1:19, 3Jn.6; προϊστάναι (-ασθαι), 1Ti.3:4 3:12 5:17; διακονεῖν, 1Ti.3:13; ἀνατρέφεσθαι, Heb.13:18; ironically, Mrk.7:9, 2Co.11:4 (but see CGT, in l); κ. ἔχειν, to be well: Mrk.16:18. Compar., κάλλιον (for superl., B1., § 44, 3), very well: Act.25:10.†\n (AS)","source_line":2763}],"occurrence_count":36,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"bem","count":35},{"gloss":"da-maneira-correta","count":1}]},"G279":{"id":"G279","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0279","disambiguated_id":"G0279 =","unique_id":"G0279","headword":"ἀμετανόητος","transliteration":"ametanoētos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"unrepentant","definition_en":"ἀμετανόητος, -ον\n (μετανοέω) \n__1. impenitent: Rom.2:5 \n __2. = ἀμεταμέλητος (π., Philo, al.; see Deiss., BS, 257; MM, VGT, see word).†\n (AS)","source_line":382}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"teu","count":1}]},"G2922":{"id":"G2922","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2922","disambiguated_id":"G2922 =","unique_id":"G2922","headword":"κριτήριον","transliteration":"kritērion","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"court/lawsuit","definition_en":"κριτήριον, -ου, τό\n (κριτής), [in LXX: 3Ki.7:7 (מִשְׁפָּט), Dan LXX TH Dan.7:10, 26, (דִּין), Su 1:49, Exo.21:6, Jdg.5:10 * ;] \n__1. a means of judging, test, criterion. \n __2. a tribunal: 1Co.6:2 6:4, Jas.2:6.†\n (AS)","source_line":3117}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"tribunais","count":2},{"gloss":"julgar","count":1}]},"G3070":{"id":"G3070","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3070","disambiguated_id":"G3070 =","unique_id":"G3070","headword":"Λυδία","transliteration":"Ludia","lexical_morphology":"N:N-F-P","gloss_en":"Lydia","definition_en":"Λυδία, -ας, ἡ \n Lydia, a woman of Thyatira: Act.16:14, 40.†\n (AS)","source_line":3272}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_po